    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MM Ward are delighted to present No. 79 Monread Heights to the market. This spacious five bedroom family home occupies an attractive corner site overlooking a green area and has been thoughtfully extended to provide generous and versatile living accommodation. The property benefits from two reception rooms, a separate utility room and a private south facing rear garden & a quiet cul-de-sac position, making it an ideal home for modern family living.\n\nUpon entering, the welcoming entrance hall features useful open understairs storage. The bright and comfortable living room benefits from an open fireplace with a mahogany surround and attractive tiled feature, creating a warm and inviting focal point. Double doors lead through to the spacious kitchen/diner, which is well proportioned and features a built-in kitchen, with a door providing access to the utility room.\n\nThe spacious utility room has a tiled floor, built-in cupboards and a window, with access to both the second reception room and the rear garden. The second reception room provides excellent additional living space and features wooden flooring, built-in units, a side door and a window overlooking the front of the property.\n\nUpstairs, the landing provides access to the attic via a Stira and also houses the hot press. The generous master bedroom features wooden flooring and benefits from a fully tiled en-suite with window, WC, WHB and walk-in electric shower. Bedroom two includes a built-in wardrobe, while bedroom three features wooden flooring and a built-in wardrobe. Bedroom Four has wooden flooring, with Bedroom Five providing further flexible accommodation. The family bathroom is fully tiled and includes a window, WC, WHB and walk-in electric shower.\n\nOutside, the front garden is fully walled and features a laid lawn, established planting and off-street parking. The property enjoys an attractive outlook over the adjoining green area. \nTo the rear, the fully walled south facing garden is a particular feature of the property, incorporating paved, stone and decked areas together with a variety of established plants and shrubbery, creating a private and pleasant space for outdoor enjoyment.\n\nThe location is a particular feature of this property, with Monread Park right on the doorstep, providing an excellent amenity for families and outdoor enthusiasts. Monread Heights is situated in a well established residential area of Naas, within easy reach of a wide range of local amenities.\n\nMonread Shopping Centre is close by and offers a wide selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday services, including Tesco Extra. Naas town centre is also within easy reach, providing an extensive choice of shopping, dining, leisure and essential services.\n\nThe area is well served by a number of schools, sporting and recreational facilities. The location also offers convenient access to the M7 motorway, making it an attractive choice for commuters, with Sallins & Naas railway station providing rail connections to Dublin and beyond.\n\nNo. 79 Monread Heights represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial five bedroom family home with generous living accommodation, valuable additional reception space and a superb south facing rear garden. Its attractive corner position, green outlook, spacious accommodation and convenient location make this a property well worth viewing.\nBER C"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall - 12'8\" (3.86m) x 6'0\" (1.83m)\nOpen understairs storage with alarm control point.\n\nLivingroom - 10'3\" (3.12m) x 14'2\" (4.32m)\nFeature fireplace with tiled surround and open fire. Double doors leading to the kitchen.\n\nKitchen\\Dining area - 10'6\" (3.2m) x 17'1\" (5.21m)\nFitted kitchen with a door leading to the utility room.\n\nUtility - 10'2\" (3.1m) x 8'3\" (2.51m)\nTiled flooring, built-in cupboards, window, door leading to the second reception room and access to the rear garden.\n\n2nd Reception room - 16'9\" (5.11m) x 10'2\" (3.1m)\nWooden flooring, built-in units, side door and window overlooking the front.\n\nLanding\nStairs leading to the attic, with access to the hot press.\n\nBathroom - 6'0\" (1.83m) x 6'0\" (1.83m)\nFully tiled with window, WC, WHB and walk-in electric shower.\n\nMaster Bedroom with ensuite - 12'2\" (3.71m) x 10'0\" (3.05m)\nWooden flooring, fully tiled walls, window, WC, WHB and walk-in electric shower.\n\nBedroom 2 - 10'3\" (3.12m) x 8'3\" (2.51m)\nBuilt-in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 3 - 10'1\" (3.07m) x 10'4\" (3.15m)\nWooden floor, Built in wardrobe\n\nBedroom 4 - 10'0\" (3.05m) x 12'6\" (3.81m)\nWooden floor.\n\nBedroom 5 - 7'11\" (2.41m) x 7'11\" (2.41m)\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
